Maybe something's wrong before fitting the model?

You can try inspectSampleCov() first. It does not fit the model, but returns the sample statistics to be analyzed.
You can then check if there is anything unusual in the sample statistics to be analyzed.

``` r
library(lavaan)
#> This is lavaan 0.6-15
#> lavaan is FREE software! Please report any bugs.
dat <- HolzingerSwineford1939
dat$x4 <- round(dat$x4)
dat$x5 <- round(dat$x5)
dat$x6 <- round(dat$x6)
HS.model <- ' visual  =~ x1 + x2 + x3
              textual =~ x4 + x5 + x6'
# Use the same arguments you would use in
# the call to sem(), but use inspectSampleCov() instead
inspectSampleCov(HS.model, data = dat, ordered = c("x4", "x5", "x6"))
#> $cov
#>       x1    x2    x3    x4    x5    x6
#> x1 1.358
#> x2 0.407 1.382
#> x3 0.580 0.451 1.275
#> x4 0.450 0.147 0.194 1.000
#> x5 0.341 0.179 0.101 0.756 1.000
#> x6 0.406 0.222 0.192 0.709 0.749 1.000
#>
#> $mean
#>    x1    x2    x3    x4    x5    x6
#> 4.936 6.088 2.250 0.000 0.000 0.000
#>
#> $th
#>  x4|t1  x4|t2  x4|t3  x4|t4  x4|t5  x4|t6  x5|t1  x5|t2  x5|t3  x5|t4  x5|t5
#> -2.328 -1.430 -0.596  0.518  1.194  1.835 -2.328 -1.228 -0.677  0.113  0.677
#>  x5|t6  x6|t1  x6|t2  x6|t3  x6|t4  x6|t5  x6|t6
#>  2.328 -2.055 -0.576  0.443  1.211  1.680  2.328
```

<sup>Created on 2023-07-01 with [reprex v2.0.2](https://reprex.tidyverse.org)</sup>

Hope this helps.

-- Shu Fai

