> I am looking to apply the testlet model by Bradlow, Wainer & Wang (1999)
> in lavaan.
>
> Under this model, the response of person i to item j Y_ij = logit^-1(t_ij)
>
> ignore the logit part, I will deal with this later, but the problem lies
> with the fact that t_ij is defined as:
>
> a_j*(theta_i  - b_j - gamma_id(j)),
>
> where a is the item discrimination, b is the difficulty, theta is the
> latent trait, gamma is the testlet effect and d is the indicator
> denoting to which of the testlets does the item belong (e.g. 1st
> testlet, 2nd testlet...).
>
> As you can see, gamma is defined not just as an item parameter, but also
> a person parameter. Thus, writing a model like this:
>
> F =~ Y1 + Y2 + Y3 + Y4 + Y5 + Y6
>
> Y1 | (b + tl1*gamma)
> Y2 | (b + tl1*gamma)
> Y3 | (b + tl1*gamma)
>
> Y4 | (b + tl2*gamma)
> Y5 | (b + tl2*gamma)
> Y6 | (b + tl2*gamma)
>
> Wouldn't work because then the testlet is going to be just an item
> parameter. What is the proper way to define this testlet model in lavaan?
>

