Perhaps the problem lies in that over time only metric equivalence is required. After all change over time is likely to appear in the intercept values.
this chapter argues for just metric equivalence in longitudinal analysis.
McArdle, J. J. (2007). Five steps in the structural factor analysis of longitudinal data. In R. Cudeck & R. C. MacCallum (Eds.), Factor analysis at 100: Historical developments and future directions (pp. 99-130). LEA.

