Hi All,

A recent GitHub issue on OpenMx (https://github.com/OpenMx/OpenMx/issues/372) reminded me of the following feature in lavaan.

The RAM representation has been added to lavaan a while ago:

https://groups.google.com/g/lavaan/c/nl5Y-HJzkxc/m/dSUSNr1BAwAJ

It seems to work even for models with user-defined variable and equality constraints. Moreover, the bug with standardized solution in 0.6-12 (https://lavaan.ugent.be/history/dot6.html) has been fixed, I believe:

``` r
library(lavaan)
#> This is lavaan 0.6-16
#> lavaan is FREE software! Please report any bugs.
HS.model <- ' visual  =~ x1 + x2 + a*x3
              textual =~ x4 + e*x5 + b*x6
              speed   =~ x7 + f*x8 + x9
              a == b
              ef := e * f'
fit1 <- cfa(HS.model, data = HolzingerSwineford1939,
            representation = "ram",
            meanstructure = TRUE)
fit2 <- cfa(HS.model, data = HolzingerSwineford1939,
            representation = "lisrel",
            meanstructure = TRUE)
identical(coef(fit1, type = "user"),
          coef(fit2, type = "user"))
#> [1] TRUE
identical(standardizedSolution(fit1),
          standardizedSolution(fit2))
#> [1] TRUE
lavInspect(fit1)
#>
#> Note: model contains equality constraints:
