Collinearity can cause even standardized coefficients to be larger than 1. It is the same phenomenon as in regression. Each of the factors that you create has multiple predictors, aside from the mediation structure you are trying to estimate. There is nothing "wrong" with these estimates, though the model is not causally identified.

