Well, that's why I wrote that this "CI" does not provide relevant information. Here are my 2 cents, if others see it differently, I'm happy to learn: the mean difference represents one effect and has one CI. A fixed parameter has no meaningful CI simply because it is fixed. You could bootstrap (for fun) the fixed parameter. With each bootstrap, the parameter is fixed and the "CI" will have no variability.

