Hi,

I agree with Shu Fai that the CI overlap approach should be taken with caution and I think that the approach Shu Fai suggests is preferable. Nevertheless, two notes:

1. The example Shu Fai uses is not entirely correct because he uses the 95% CI rather than the 84% CI:
est2 <- parameterEstimates(fit2, level = 0.95)

est2[4, "ci.upper"] > est2[26, "ci.lower"]
#> [1] TRUE

est2 <- parameterEstimates(fit2, level = 0.84)

est2[4, "ci.upper"] > est2[26, "ci.lower"]

#> [1] FALSE

2. The linked article contains only a few statements about the parameterization of the model. Just ask the authors what exactly they did. I would be interested in that as well :-)

Best

Christian

