Hi Shu Fai,

taken from the contribution Jazzi linked: "As Tryon (2001) has shown, in case of two (or more) independent samples two 84% condence intervals correspond to a two-sided signicance test on the 5% level. If the condence intervals do not overlap, they differ signicantly" (page 336).

Best

Christian
